menuconfig ARCH_REALTEK
	bool "Realtek SoCs"
	depends on ARCH_MULTI_V7
	select ARM_ERRATA_814220
	select ARM_GIC
	select ARM_GLOBAL_TIMER
	select CLKSRC_ARM_GLOBAL_TIMER_SCHED_CLOCK
	select GENERIC_IRQ_CHIP
	select RESET_CONTROLLER
	help
	  This enables support for the Realtek RTD1195 SoC family.

	  RTD1195 is a Cortex-A7 r0p5 part, one of the revisions (r0p2-r0p5)
	  affected by erratum 814220 (L2 set/way cache maintenance can
	  overtake L1). The erratum itself isn't SMP-specific - it can bite
	  any full cache flush, single core or not - but on this board it
	  surfaced as an intermittent early-boot memory corruption tied to
	  CPU1 coming up under heavy concurrent vmalloc/vmap_area churn
	  (systemd + friends), so ARM_ERRATA_814220 is force-selected here
	  rather than left as an opt-in.
